{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"id\":\"notion://docs/notion-flavored-markdown-spec\",\"title\":\"Notion-flavored Markdown Specification\",\"text\":\"# Notion-flavored Markdown\\n\\nCommonMark + GFM tables, task lists, strikethrough; custom emoji :smile:; inline math $...$; display math uses bare $$ lines around the equation (never same-line $$...$$ or \\\\[...\\\\]); citations [^URL] only (no footnotes). Notion XML tags below. Never write other HTML tags (e.g. <div>, <details>, <figure>, <small>, <sup>, <sub>, <mark>); they are saved as literal text.\\n\\nRules:\\n- Escape literal tags in text as \\\\<tag> or &lt;tag&gt;; never inside code or mention labels, which are already literal.\\n- Always fence code blocks; never indent them. One-copyable-block rule: make the opening and closing fence longer than the longest backtick run in the content. Triple-backtick content requires four-backtick outer fences; never use triple backticks both outside and inside.\\n- Hard line break = trailing \\\\ replacing the space before it. Empty paragraph = <p />.\\n- Blocks (tables, lists, headings, etc.) start on new lines after blank lines, never inline.\\n\\nInline tags:\\n- <b>, <i>, <s>, <u> (the only underline); required when styled text has leading/trailing spaces.\\n- <span color=\\\"...\\\" discussion-urls=\\\"url,url\\\">text</span>; nest to combine: <span color=\\\"orange\\\"><u>word</u></span>.\\n- Use <mention url=\\\"...\\\">Label</mention> or <mention url=\\\"...\\\" /> for mentioning Notion entities user://..., HTTPS page URLs, collection://..., agent://..., group://.... Database mentions use type=\\\"database\\\" to distinguish them from page mentions. Regular links use [text](url).\\n- <date start=\\\"YYYY-MM-DD\\\" end=\\\"YYYY-MM-DD\\\" start-time=\\\"HH:mm\\\" end-time=\\\"HH:mm\\\" time-zone=\\\"IANA_TZ\\\" />\\n- <link-preview url=\\\"...\\\" source=\\\"...\\\" /> is a read-only marker. Preserve it when editing existing content; never add one to create a link preview.\\n\\nBlock tags: always use the tag form when a block needs attributes, children, or edge whitespace — <quote> not >, <li> not -. Most accept color=\\\"gray|brown|orange|yellow|green|blue|purple|pink|red\\\" (text) or _bg forms like \\\"blue_bg\\\" (background). Color a whole block or cell with its color attribute; use <span color> only for words inside text.\\n\\nOne container shape for <p>, <h1>-<h4>, <quote>, <toggle heading=\\\"h1|h2|h3|h4\\\" color=\\\"...\\\">, <li color=\\\"...\\\"> in <ul>/<ol type=\\\"1|a|i\\\">, <column> in <columns>, <tab icon=\\\"emoji or Notion Icon\\\"> in <tabs>, <mail to=\\\"...\\\" cc=\\\"...\\\" bcc=\\\"...\\\" from=\\\"...\\\" subject=\\\"...\\\" attachments=\\\"url,url\\\">, <meeting-notes>:\\n\\n<quote color=\\\"purple_bg\\\">\\nTitle text\\n\\n- child bullet\\n\\n<callout icon=\\\"💡\\\" color=\\\"yellow_bg\\\">\\nCallout body child\\n</callout>\\n</quote>\\n\\nThe title/label is body text right after the opening tag, never an attribute. Children follow a blank line — plain Markdown, no <p> wrappers or > prefixes. Blank lines touching the opening or closing tags become stray whitespace; never pad. <p /> = empty title.\\n\\nPlain <h1>-<h4> have no children: nested blocks become siblings. For children, use <toggle heading=\\\"h1|h2|h3|h4\\\">.\\n\\nOther blocks:\\n- <todo checked=\\\"true|false\\\"> when a todo needs color; else - [ ] / - [x].\\n- <equation color=\\\"...\\\">x + y = z</equation>\\n- <table-of-contents color=\\\"...\\\" />\\n- Media (body = optional caption): ![caption](url), or <image source=\\\"...\\\" color=\\\"...\\\">caption</image> for attributes; other embeds use their type's tag: <pdf source=\\\"...\\\">caption</pdf>, likewise <file>, <audio>, <video>, <bookmark>, <embed>. Each image must be its own block: never inline it with text (paragraph, list-item, etc.) or another image, and separate consecutive images with a blank line. Use <external_object_instance integration=\\\"github|figma|google_drive\\\">Embed name</external_object_instance> to create a rich integration embed placeholder.\\n- To create an HTML block, call notion-create-attachment with the HTML content and a filename ending in .html. Insert its suggested_markdown with notion-create-pages or notion-update-page to render the attachment with <embed>.\\n- <page url=\\\"...\\\" color=\\\"...\\\">Title</page>; represents a subpage on the current page. Warning: an update_page call that leaves out this tag deletes the subpage when allow_deleting_content is true. Otherwise the update fails with an error that lists the subpages. Omit url only when creating a new subpage.\\n- <folder url=\\\"...\\\">Title</folder>; represents an existing folder. Use fetch to read its immediate children, then follow nested folder URLs to continue traversing. Preserve the tag unless intentionally moving or deleting the folder; folders cannot be created from Markdown.\\n- <database url=\\\"...\\\" data-source-url=\\\"...\\\" inline=\\\"true|false\\\" icon=\\\"emoji\\\" wiki=\\\"true|false\\\" color=\\\"...\\\">Title</database>; same url/title rules. Wiki databases set wiki=\\\"true\\\"; their pages use parent type \\\"page\\\" with the wiki page URL, not \\\"dataSource\\\".\\n- <synced-block url=\\\"...\\\">...</synced-block> is an original synced block; omit url for new. <synced-block-reference url=\\\"...\\\" notice=\\\"...\\\">...</synced-block-reference> shows an original from elsewhere. Copy its url from an existing <synced-block> or <synced-block-reference>; a page url is never valid, so a whole page cannot be synced. If no such url is available, don't add a reference (even an empty one) or a note; tell the user why in your reply. To add a reference, leave it empty. Content inside a new reference replaces the original's content everywhere it appears. Only edit the children of a reference that's already on the page, and only to change the original.\\n- <meeting-notes attendees=\\\"user://id,...\\\" view-url=\\\"...\\\" legacy=\\\"true\\\">Title<meeting-notes-section-notes>Notes</meeting-notes-section-notes><meeting-notes-section-summary>Summary</meeting-notes-section-summary></meeting-notes>; content outside <meeting-notes-section-notes> is ignored; omit view-url, legacy, and the summary section for new. legacy=\\\"true\\\" marks an older meeting notes block that isn't a page; keep it as is. An existing <meeting-notes> may also have an optional read-only <meeting-notes-section-transcript> child: a \\\"Transcript omitted\\\" body means the transcript was not loaded, so follow its instructions to load it; never edit its contents, and never add it to new meeting notes.\\n- <custom-block definition-id=\\\"UUID\\\" url=\\\"...\\\" />; places an instance of a custom block definition deployed in this workspace. Use a self-closing tag on its own line; the instance inherits the definition's bindings. Omit url for a new instance; readback adds its instance URL. Preserve that URL when editing, reordering, or moving an existing instance.\\n- Columns: <columns><column ratio=\\\"50\\\">...</column><column ratio=\\\"50\\\">...</column></columns>. ratio is an optional percentage of the column-list width.\\n\\nTables:\\n- Pipe tables (escape | in cells as \\\\|) for plain tables; <table> only for styled ones; never mix the two.\\n- <table fit-page-width=\\\"true|false\\\" header-row=\\\"true|false\\\" header-column=\\\"true|false\\\">, optional <colgroup><col width=\\\"180\\\" color=\\\"...\\\" /></colgroup>, <tr color=\\\"...\\\"> rows, <th>/<td color=\\\"...\\\"> cells.\\n- Cells are inline-only (<br /> for line breaks); copy the existing cells' formatting when adding rows (pad with blank lines if the existing cells do).\",\"url\":\"notion://docs/notion-flavored-markdown-spec\",\"metadata\":{\"type\":\"documentation\"}}"}],"structuredContent":{"id":"notion://docs/notion-flavored-markdown-spec","title":"Notion-flavored Markdown Specification","text":"# Notion-flavored Markdown\n\nCommonMark + GFM tables, task lists, strikethrough; custom emoji :smile:; inline math $...$; display math uses bare $$ lines around the equation (never same-line $$...$$ or \\[...\\]); citations [^URL] only (no footnotes). Notion XML tags below. Never write other HTML tags (e.g. <div>, <details>, <figure>, <small>, <sup>, <sub>, <mark>); they are saved as literal text.\n\nRules:\n- Escape literal tags in text as \\<tag> or &lt;tag&gt;; never inside code or mention labels, which are already literal.\n- Always fence code blocks; never indent them. One-copyable-block rule: make the opening and closing fence longer than the longest backtick run in the content. Triple-backtick content requires four-backtick outer fences; never use triple backticks both outside and inside.\n- Hard line break = trailing \\ replacing the space before it. Empty paragraph = <p />.\n- Blocks (tables, lists, headings, etc.) start on new lines after blank lines, never inline.\n\nInline tags:\n- <b>, <i>, <s>, <u> (the only underline); required when styled text has leading/trailing spaces.\n- <span color=\"...\" discussion-urls=\"url,url\">text</span>; nest to combine: <span color=\"orange\"><u>word</u></span>.\n- Use <mention url=\"...\">Label</mention> or <mention url=\"...\" /> for mentioning Notion entities user://..., HTTPS page URLs, collection://..., agent://..., group://.... Database mentions use type=\"database\" to distinguish them from page mentions. Regular links use [text](url).\n- <date start=\"YYYY-MM-DD\" end=\"YYYY-MM-DD\" start-time=\"HH:mm\" end-time=\"HH:mm\" time-zone=\"IANA_TZ\" />\n- <link-preview url=\"...\" source=\"...\" /> is a read-only marker. Preserve it when editing existing content; never add one to create a link preview.\n\nBlock tags: always use the tag form when a block needs attributes, children, or edge whitespace — <quote> not >, <li> not -. Most accept color=\"gray|brown|orange|yellow|green|blue|purple|pink|red\" (text) or _bg forms like \"blue_bg\" (background). Color a whole block or cell with its color attribute; use <span color> only for words inside text.\n\nOne container shape for <p>, <h1>-<h4>, <quote>, <toggle heading=\"h1|h2|h3|h4\" color=\"...\">, <li color=\"...\"> in <ul>/<ol type=\"1|a|i\">, <column> in <columns>, <tab icon=\"emoji or Notion Icon\"> in <tabs>, <mail to=\"...\" cc=\"...\" bcc=\"...\" from=\"...\" subject=\"...\" attachments=\"url,url\">, <meeting-notes>:\n\n<quote color=\"purple_bg\">\nTitle text\n\n- child bullet\n\n<callout icon=\"💡\" color=\"yellow_bg\">\nCallout body child\n</callout>\n</quote>\n\nThe title/label is body text right after the opening tag, never an attribute. Children follow a blank line — plain Markdown, no <p> wrappers or > prefixes. Blank lines touching the opening or closing tags become stray whitespace; never pad. <p /> = empty title.\n\nPlain <h1>-<h4> have no children: nested blocks become siblings. For children, use <toggle heading=\"h1|h2|h3|h4\">.\n\nOther blocks:\n- <todo checked=\"true|false\"> when a todo needs color; else - [ ] / - [x].\n- <equation color=\"...\">x + y = z</equation>\n- <table-of-contents color=\"...\" />\n- Media (body = optional caption): ![caption](url), or <image source=\"...\" color=\"...\">caption</image> for attributes; other embeds use their type's tag: <pdf source=\"...\">caption</pdf>, likewise <file>, <audio>, <video>, <bookmark>, <embed>. Each image must be its own block: never inline it with text (paragraph, list-item, etc.) or another image, and separate consecutive images with a blank line. Use <external_object_instance integration=\"github|figma|google_drive\">Embed name</external_object_instance> to create a rich integration embed placeholder.\n- To create an HTML block, call notion-create-attachment with the HTML content and a filename ending in .html. Insert its suggested_markdown with notion-create-pages or notion-update-page to render the attachment with <embed>.\n- <page url=\"...\" color=\"...\">Title</page>; represents a subpage on the current page. Warning: an update_page call that leaves out this tag deletes the subpage when allow_deleting_content is true. Otherwise the update fails with an error that lists the subpages. Omit url only when creating a new subpage.\n- <folder url=\"...\">Title</folder>; represents an existing folder. Use fetch to read its immediate children, then follow nested folder URLs to continue traversing. Preserve the tag unless intentionally moving or deleting the folder; folders cannot be created from Markdown.\n- <database url=\"...\" data-source-url=\"...\" inline=\"true|false\" icon=\"emoji\" wiki=\"true|false\" color=\"...\">Title</database>; same url/title rules. Wiki databases set wiki=\"true\"; their pages use parent type \"page\" with the wiki page URL, not \"dataSource\".\n- <synced-block url=\"...\">...</synced-block> is an original synced block; omit url for new. <synced-block-reference url=\"...\" notice=\"...\">...</synced-block-reference> shows an original from elsewhere. Copy its url from an existing <synced-block> or <synced-block-reference>; a page url is never valid, so a whole page cannot be synced. If no such url is available, don't add a reference (even an empty one) or a note; tell the user why in your reply. To add a reference, leave it empty. Content inside a new reference replaces the original's content everywhere it appears. Only edit the children of a reference that's already on the page, and only to change the original.\n- <meeting-notes attendees=\"user://id,...\" view-url=\"...\" legacy=\"true\">Title<meeting-notes-section-notes>Notes</meeting-notes-section-notes><meeting-notes-section-summary>Summary</meeting-notes-section-summary></meeting-notes>; content outside <meeting-notes-section-notes> is ignored; omit view-url, legacy, and the summary section for new. legacy=\"true\" marks an older meeting notes block that isn't a page; keep it as is. An existing <meeting-notes> may also have an optional read-only <meeting-notes-section-transcript> child: a \"Transcript omitted\" body means the transcript was not loaded, so follow its instructions to load it; never edit its contents, and never add it to new meeting notes.\n- <custom-block definition-id=\"UUID\" url=\"...\" />; places an instance of a custom block definition deployed in this workspace. Use a self-closing tag on its own line; the instance inherits the definition's bindings. Omit url for a new instance; readback adds its instance URL. Preserve that URL when editing, reordering, or moving an existing instance.\n- Columns: <columns><column ratio=\"50\">...</column><column ratio=\"50\">...</column></columns>. ratio is an optional percentage of the column-list width.\n\nTables:\n- Pipe tables (escape | in cells as \\|) for plain tables; <table> only for styled ones; never mix the two.\n- <table fit-page-width=\"true|false\" header-row=\"true|false\" header-column=\"true|false\">, optional <colgroup><col width=\"180\" color=\"...\" /></colgroup>, <tr color=\"...\"> rows, <th>/<td color=\"...\"> cells.\n- Cells are inline-only (<br /> for line breaks); copy the existing cells' formatting when adding rows (pad with blank lines if the existing cells do).","url":"notion://docs/notion-flavored-markdown-spec","metadata":{"type":"documentation"}},"isError":false}
